WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:07.080
Hey David, is it now time for Bernie or Warren
to drop out because Joe Biden is still in

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:11.209
the lead and we as progressives need to take
him out.

00:00:11.209 --> 00:00:15.339
So listen, I've answered this a couple of
times before and it's been a few months so

00:00:15.339 --> 00:00:18.700
I'm glad to address it again because we're
further into the democratic primary at this

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.010
point.

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:24.850
What exactly would be the point of Bernie
or Warren dropping out as the question is

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:30.250
asked here, the point would be we don't want
Biden to win cause he's not a progressive.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:34.079
Bernie and Warren are the two Progressive's
with the best shot.

00:00:34.079 --> 00:00:36.859
If one drops out, it helps the other.

00:00:36.859 --> 00:00:40.429
It takes out Biden and then we laugh all the
way to the bank.

00:00:40.429 --> 00:00:41.429
Okay.

00:00:41.429 --> 00:00:46.940
The problem with this is the math of it and
the math of it is I reviewed earlier today,

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.120
still doesn't really favor this strategy.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.820
You know, I got a, I did a live stream, uh,
over the weekend on Twitch and I got a phone

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:58.309
call from someone who said, Hey David, you
know, I want, I think it was Bernie to win

00:00:58.309 --> 00:00:59.309
or something like that.

00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:05.040
I want Bernie to win, but if Bernie doesn't
win Iowa, should I maybe look at switching

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:10.550
my vote when I vote in New York state, the
caller was in New York state voter and I said,

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:13.960
guys, you're getting way ahead of yourselves
here.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:16.320
You don't need to do anything like that.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.041
Nothing is going to be, there's one way in
which those first four primaries, Iowa and

00:01:21.041 --> 00:01:27.070
New Hampshire, Nevada and South Carolina will
really sort of quote, decide the winner, which

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:32.730
is if one person sweeps all of them and does
it really handily like with overwhelming numbers,

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:34.980
which is not likely to happen at this point.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:35.980
Okay.

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:40.860
The most likely scenario is that no matter
what happens in those first four primaries,

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:45.200
it's still going to be a fight into March
3rd I think March 3rd is super.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:49.520
Tuesday, there's like 14 primaries on March
3rd maybe super Tuesday is actually a different

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:54.460
date, but there's a huge chunk of votes that
are going to be coming after those four primaries.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:55.460
Okay.

00:01:55.460 --> 00:02:01.630
Any, anyone will almost likely, uh, be able
to win after those first four support.

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:02.630
Who you like?

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:07.700
If it's Bernie or Warren, that's totally fine
because here's the math about Bernie and Warren.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:08.700
Okay.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:15.300
Uh, Warren supporters have Bernie as their
second choice, but only by three points over

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.300
Biden.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:17.300
Okay.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:20.240
Meaning that for every hundred, I believe
I'm going by the numbers.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:25.840
I recall for every hundred Warren supporters
that changed their minds.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:31.741
Or if Warren bails go to their second choice
candidate for every hundred, I think 28 go

00:02:31.741 --> 00:02:35.020
to Bernie and 25 go to Biden.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.020
Okay.

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:38.520
That's not enough for Bernie to close the
gap.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:39.680
If Warren quits.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:42.500
All right, now let's look at the other option.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:45.220
Bernie quits Bernie supporters.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:51.510
Now, according to the latest morning consult
poll, Bernie supporters have Biden as their

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:58.610
top choice by two points over Warren, I think
it's like 28 to 26 so if Bernie quits for

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:05.090
every hundred of his supporters that go to
their second choice, Biden builds a lead over

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:06.349
Elizabeth Warren.

00:03:06.349 --> 00:03:07.349
Okay?

00:03:07.349 --> 00:03:14.060
If either drops out, they help each other
and Biden roughly equally so the math doesn't

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:20.900
support the strategy of Bernie quitting to
help Warren or Warren quitting to help Bernie.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:25.980
Now you could say, well, those might be the
second choices as of now, but if one quits

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:30.180
and endorses the other, then it'll shift those
numbers.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:34.050
It may shift the numbers to some degree, but
we're just talking about the primaries here

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:37.880
and it, it, I, I, my prediction is it would
not shift it as much as you imagined.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.599
So let's just all go out.

00:03:40.599 --> 00:03:44.730
If you're an Iowa voter, you're going to get
the first crack at it.

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:47.950
Go out and vote, whoever you actually support.

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:53.379
If you're a New Hampshire voter and Iowa doesn't
go the way you want, go out and vote for whoever

00:03:53.379 --> 00:03:55.860
you actually support in New Hampshire.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:59.550
If one person wins Iowa and another one's
new who wins New Hampshire and then it's time

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:02.629
for Nevada, I believe is the third primary.

00:04:02.629 --> 00:04:05.850
Go out and vote for whoever you like in Nevada.

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:07.720
This is going to sort itself out.

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:15.349
There is so much time for consolidation in
the Bernie Warren, uh, supporter groups that

00:04:15.349 --> 00:04:20.109
these are not the things we should be to the,
the candidates who are in the top three should

00:04:20.109 --> 00:04:21.470
not drop out.

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:25.240
There's a whole bunch of people at the bottom
that need to go because they've got no shot

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:29.570
and they're just a distraction on the stage,
but it is not time for Bernie to drop out.

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:31.460
It is not a time for Warren to drop out.

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:36.600
Why would someone in the top three who is
right in there within a few points of being

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:39.340
in the lead of this thing drop out at this
point in time?

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:44.670
My suggestion is that we stopped talking about
that and focus on the important things like

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:49.780
substantive debates, figuring out exactly
how each person will pay for their healthcare

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:55.150
plan and clearing the stage of some of the
hangers on that have no chance whatsoever

00:04:55.150 --> 00:05:00.000
of winning and are contributing nothing other
than giving the people who have a shot time

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.380
to sip water as they wait for the next question
to come to them.

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:05.560
You disagree with me, let me know.

